WEBVTT

00:00:00.351 --> 00:00:11.404
A planned request can now merge into work that has already started, finished, or been archived. Merge with opens a searchable list: planned tasks first, then work in progress, done, and archived.

00:00:12.362 --> 00:00:24.007
Here the request belongs to CSV export, which is already in progress. An agent compares the request with that card and its handover summary. The existing work is preserved, and the owner checks the result.

00:00:25.051 --> 00:00:35.279
The request is covered completely. Its text is crossed out on the left; the right card and merged result are identical. Approve merge removes the duplicate request and keeps the in-progress card.

00:00:36.392 --> 00:00:47.340
This second request asks for both CSV and Excel. Only an unworked request can dissolve; the card already in progress remains the survivor. The agent identifies which work is still missing.

00:00:52.344 --> 00:01:03.246
CSV is crossed out as covered, while Excel remains. Below the unchanged result, a new planned follow-up contains only the Excel work. Separate leaves both originals as they were and creates nothing.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:09.791
Merging the originals again gives a fresh comparison. Nothing is removed or created while the owner checks it.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:21.145
Only the missing Excel work becomes a planned task. Approval creates it beside the survivor, with a wait arrow. The in-progress export remains unchanged.

00:01:22.124 --> 00:01:34.384
An archived card can also be the survivor. This request includes PDF, already delivered, plus HTML. The review preserves the archived PDF card and proposes only the missing HTML export.

00:01:35.351 --> 00:01:45.487
Only the missing HTML work becomes a follow-up. Approval creates that planned task, while the original PDF export stays archived with its text and handover preserved.

00:01:46.445 --> 00:01:57.358
Two requests nobody has worked on still become one combined task. Even when a planned task selects a proposal, the planned task survives. The owner can approve the combined text or separate the cards.

00:02:00.169 --> 00:02:11.257
The combined task includes both the preview and its row count. Approve merge keeps that complete text in the planned task. Across every state, the owner checks what stays and what becomes follow-up work.
